[{"id":"VRCE-2-35-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":1,"english":"Then exceedingly distressed, Rāma, Sītā and Lakşmaņa, bowing down to the king, circumambulated him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"55a34fa76d46d17150aa0a767edb92d0184c577a8e542161b595c356b9a66aed","compact":"b671a2fce727d301202d7d403f0e39679f0a1ca1305195bc213c5eed5da781b5","nasal":"b99079a4810a67c31f011c87ef18e10b3fe1f14a9f5a8c8557f9619c23320d97"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":2,"english":"Then with the king's permission, the righteous Rāghava, stupefied with sorrow, in company with Sītā, paid respects to his mother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.604,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e414e676f20fe938d64305abf8a9354f58340e7017b8582ac8c9e02b3b3ae8bd","compact":"fb49d84d3afbdb26e39ccd2f385d12dc4a0afa8fa3c8341f321508ca0f8be933","nasal":"fb49d84d3afbdb26e39ccd2f385d12dc4a0afa8fa3c8341f321508ca0f8be933"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":3,"english":"Following his brother, Lakşmaņa saluted Kausalyā; then he again took hold of his mother Sumitrā's feet.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e43a320d66cbf8c4f0f69563ddde01eae55b2764841e1ba69f515bf1d9c01e6","compact":"03aa2ca62a575410628d13cc3936ed93999fe90768088f9b0556306860afa4d3","nasal":"03aa2ca62a575410628d13cc3936ed93999fe90768088f9b0556306860afa4d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":4,"english":"As the son of Sumitrā was thus engaged in honouring his mother, his mother smelling the crown of his head, thus spoke to the mightyarmed Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"762babaf4c7cc9ca26888d4e418e921874314ebec90f7db128e512b1f43fba53","compact":"a7bcd6c0a5d2bfa2a783f712ba0b6c8b55cc5a8e03849c2a725e7da1f3c21fa0","nasal":"9c69398040146c662256428df8f8c288643d24154ade7bde33df1b730c5ecb0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":5,"english":"Although attached to your friends here, you have my permission to go to the forest. When Rama shall have gone (to the woods), do not, O son, show any negligence to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffecebc5512b6e034278f7b0c4e02e5bf6ff5b04aace128fcba3af0a4509d030","compact":"27be3cb5c7d28ea08d93992a65fb2547ec649db5140b3149e18d40bc8e266454","nasal":"27be3cb5c7d28ea08d93992a65fb2547ec649db5140b3149e18d40bc8e266454"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":6,"english":"O sinless one, whether in prosperity or in adversity, even this one is your way. That a younger brother should follow his elder is in this world the duty of the righteous.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"35ff9868218f1b8bd56b001d33836875f0548a03da6c522b9fd883d6c3d42b77","compact":"8939af7476ddd00e12492ff1357f526c84e394cc3692e62991466dd584fb3406","nasal":"8939af7476ddd00e12492ff1357f526c84e394cc3692e62991466dd584fb3406"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":7,"english":"These are the legitimate duties ever observed by this race, charity, initiation into sacrifice, and renunciation of the body in the field of battle,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.983,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c40834a4c9c9caa4817cb68834bbda559c08f9c6ec67521aabcc069f0f61710f","compact":"082fa155c5a7f07a791c199e403f977af16bf8d479eae7b1086833a93ed4562b","nasal":"082fa155c5a7f07a791c199e403f977af16bf8d479eae7b1086833a93ed4562b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":8,"english":"Do you consider Rāma as Daśaratha, and Janaka's own-begotten as myself; do you regard Ayodhyā as a wilderness, go my son, at your sweet pleasure. Having thus spoken to that dear descendant of Raghu, who had made up his mind (to journey to the forest), Sumitra again and again said to him, “Go! Go!\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.934,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e4d920c7aead22eb884b4acaab8056c806b5999e121a65c1a328f8c4139f9c74","compact":"5763afd580efdcf1ba98170cbc11567d175108dc5095a4853d9ca6dbc08f3ce4","nasal":"5763afd580efdcf1ba98170cbc11567d175108dc5095a4853d9ca6dbc08f3ce4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":9,"english":"Then like to Mātali addressing Väsava, that one understanding humility, Sumantra, with joined hands humbly said to Kākutstha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae15266339a918d0b499bba3d2128cd72d5d6630ebfaad2f4b087c5607dadbae","compact":"1d91b5a9b774fddf0753014143d2bed351d635f0d55b9bc5ebdc89fa32d63400","nasal":"0cad53a72d86283e9c42c80fe4a7dbc05a04c62cb55daca208f762e013d5e476"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":10,"english":"O illustrious prince, good betide you: do you ascend the car. O Rāma, I will speedily take you to wherever you will tell me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.985,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1eebcd25c64a037a9773363ad4704832ba447935666a67aa877f3b7799a2b6b4","compact":"72e92817331252e5b65623ab9b1d7eefc7bd6cb8317b65f26c76f3747403b921","nasal":"72e92817331252e5b65623ab9b1d7eefc7bd6cb8317b65f26c76f3747403b921"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":11,"english":"You will have to spend fourteen years in the forest, and your stay must commence from this very day. So the noble lady has ordered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"767f838db14a7f07f72874c5cf125e7b1779a7f39c70c420e64575e5e5143851","compact":"cc279a3af1e911e2ad9c0bc7b74a72330e9eb320247c9c3695b2528ae019f74b","nasal":"cc279a3af1e911e2ad9c0bc7b74a72330e9eb320247c9c3695b2528ae019f74b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":12,"english":"Then having adorned her person, that best of her sex, Sītā, with a glad heart ascended the car resembling the sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c5aa0fb1ed0eb3a52715b2636a9b43bc606a5ddb341561a75c9b5d2dc1ee50a","compact":"2aab9f87e7190404b77b3ae297d26a1f6b3c97ed974626878d5666be2a020085","nasal":"2aab9f87e7190404b77b3ae297d26a1f6b3c97ed974626878d5666be2a020085"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":13,"english":"And then he placed in front of the car various weapons, coats of mail, a basket bound in hide and a hoe, At length the brothers Rama and Laks maņa swiftly ascended the flaming car garnished with gold.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a7fafd1b2a39fc1c3f87737ace1155e4a6d004ba148869f2fe3cd147b52e19d","compact":"384da15f5ab43ac7009f7097b792e2faa69e0127968508cdd75465e27b6319d3","nasal":"384da15f5ab43ac7009f7097b792e2faa69e0127968508cdd75465e27b6319d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":14,"english":"And seeing them with Sītā for the third, mounted, Sumantra drove the car yoked with goodly horses resembling the wind in celerity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.627,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"71521ab8ff81b0a121a91f6b2aae0dd44bd9698fc082bfa0a443277207af3325","compact":"72722651b1997b3798be928d757baf4e1d7e84abaf9ce8edc1a32f40928812f7","nasal":"4836c464d6040f98846933ca566c3b9b001d0c2a6ce7391c1c7290c344f9b676"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":15,"english":"On Rāghava having left for the forest to stay there for a long period, the men and beasts within the city were deprived of their senses (by grief).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6978bc3dbb3e70e62bb0bdc96dd0e813645770d3ca9160f817997a76a3fbb932","compact":"a4c9abcc147d02da666c50d44169a8cae7ddf430997fd9a78556ce1d60c0acc2","nasal":"a4c9abcc147d02da666c50d44169a8cae7ddf430997fd9a78556ce1d60c0acc2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":16,"english":"And in the city there arose a mighty tumult in consequence of the hurrying of people, the elephants waxing mad and furious, and the neighings of horses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a6cd4576018261338107bb47797e9daf5653badc2f76fb7d0bd5e21dd8a2382","compact":"0a0e55f82afdb051c8d26b7da23c927b3faf68ade311e86655241bad7eece100","nasal":"9afeb13d5a5edac1e3582b8801b89b72d58905b04458d1e8899e4df757438103"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":17,"english":"And the entire city containing, young and old, extremely afflicted, rushed after Rāma, like persons oppressed with the heat of the sun rushing towards water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25223350e0e4a2fae628333d23f87ce905832e569cef8c758db49b90534618a2","compact":"616df3f0889ab25e480367a0e1fee198ecb8aa6b9a6388ad3826cd9b82b812cd","nasal":"616df3f0889ab25e480367a0e1fee198ecb8aa6b9a6388ad3826cd9b82b812cd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":18,"english":"As his side and back, the people bending forward with their faces covered with the vapour of grief, and sighing hard, said to he charioteer.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.819,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3906f6e4cbb0e2ca7efe9b917102922bd8ebd15018330fcf168b4c2616e9d536","compact":"6cc007042925a76a9f25f6b797804d9c3492936bfa811458c1491a2d6fd882c3","nasal":"5dd6fff71c54afb48b0c3b52cf05b62f5c6173df188f31f11ef8e82b5a28d654"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":19,"english":"O charioteer, rein in the horses, do you proceed softly. We will see the countenance of Rāma, which we shall never see again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac801276607c50b96aa2ca962f4b076299a38425f5ed7dae2f0083178e0b2c55","compact":"477c81aba8f4563105d3dfb29adadbdac643941888597db18e3f190c98dfb9f6","nasal":"477c81aba8f4563105d3dfb29adadbdac643941888597db18e3f190c98dfb9f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":20,"english":"Surely the heart of Rāma's mother is made of iron, for it does not burst on witnessing her son resembling Skanda repairing to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad24e000f03720c7025109c77b116a9c5f28f4f03649b1cb6b58bda1c652f6db","compact":"6a06b185d6b32affa66efb160dccac60dc248e5bb60cc4c73b60578b2401d64e","nasal":"6a06b185d6b32affa66efb160dccac60dc248e5bb60cc4c73b60578b2401d64e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":21,"english":"Vaidehī, attaining her desire, follows her husband, like a shadow, attached to virtue, she does not forsake him, even as the Sun forsakes not Meru.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c6c175d83da0c1878d23a1b3800527930d7430bc64769a31f3a794984ca47b5e","compact":"7a7db97b2abee7b0e5a5478d0c9de1f159fdc488bdc7986c53fb89d1b2920bd0","nasal":"7a7db97b2abee7b0e5a5478d0c9de1f159fdc488bdc7986c53fb89d1b2920bd0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":22,"english":"O Laksmana, you are blessed, since you will serve your god-like brother ever speaking fair.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59b63cdbde1f13b74ad70c1328ffdaba6ddaeda674f19b55e4373755daf22615","compact":"7fd936d75ae37335b88b3b7f35caf0f430769d8339c3bc054c6f788413ccb102","nasal":"16ce11a601cc406fe6b631f8618d312591283d397af7685e3d77726a3cb7b67d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":23,"english":"This design of yours is great; this is your mighty good fortune; this is the way to heaven that you are following him. Saying this; they could not suppress their fears; and the men followed the beloved descendant of Ikşvāku.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.537,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-24","DUTT-2-40-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c616d2034e5ab03707dd05d0e526b5d3f99f362ce7616f404e29ed2dc0eb4ec1","compact":"2be6c0f42ceb699f561b201288a5aa2975b93a113c972447245f0486a342b67d","nasal":"f1b4aa4cd2b6a90f69b0a3037d03e75f0d564677912dc541fe49ff9dba092cab"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":24,"english":"Then the king, his sense overcome by grief, surrounded by his distressed wives, went out of his house, saying, “I will behold my dear son.”","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e4f5eb8e426425a1e60d034455e034fabf23176d2856cf034556e5e1e9cc968f","compact":"6e7ad65c81733bef9840f97540dd976f617d77e0d49a045e82391611a44f2438","nasal":"6e7ad65c81733bef9840f97540dd976f617d77e0d49a045e82391611a44f2438"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":25,"english":"He heard before him a mighty noise proceeding from weeping women, like to the roars of she-elephants, when a great elephant has been taken captive.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6fff7f574fbfcec3d771f8dc473824bb9ba42f8710b721b3167e31a539fe103f","compact":"b251f1ef2741c4b831877a34ed03d186c5f0b79b8c720ef58df4450bd01d02cd","nasal":"b0c59b028091270942b848d63880dad8b8c12bd03e489884af7b023dac71dde8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":26,"english":"Thereupon Rāma's father, the graceful Kākutstha, became shorn of his splendour, like to the full-moon enveloped at the appointed time during the eclipse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.923,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0fa11a88d2f256b5daf029007f715eaa3ee0c308c2c438427d676221d46050ff","compact":"3c3ba881605f5c6d8cd4c1b67bb876a9c85516b4f320edf1e91061125992e0ef","nasal":"4cb0118ae27aafdc5b52443efcad009cdc65c1dc4862d8f5e4f407bc740a2c08"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":27,"english":"Then seeing the sovereign senseless and stricken with exceeding sorrow, the multitudes at the rear of Rāma broke out into a loud tumult.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb647bdc3790803fd0e6399b2dcb7a54241dbd66447479a12fcf38f21013fbdf","compact":"35ae31e8ef127c3b90c1eed1815b310a9d797ea5ef592e174f307acc2451b997","nasal":"11ff61ef7331851f62e970bb2e6c5e892b7d8d1452c185964a0d5582f8590dc4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":28,"english":"And seeing the king weeping aloud with the inmates of the inner apartment, some exclaiming \"Oh Rama,\" and others, “O Rāma's mother,\" began to be-wail.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0f4c17fc4a4093a62587b6a6d897968d1bc9d7d55ef7c2cb26f42512c42c550","