"sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84e4cf8274e682a91e87721b97d6a4dcedaa8dedfb8e798f893436ca7be15fd7","compact":"60a250a7146c4a34bf0264aec668664157c66fd74dfbdee4472a5bad6b4f5ef5","nasal":"60a250a7146c4a34bf0264aec668664157c66fd74dfbdee4472a5bad6b4f5ef5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":32,"english":"Rāma beheld his mother Kausalyā running after the car, bewailing aloud, “Rāma, Rāma, Ah Sītā, Lakşmaņa,” shedding tears for Rāma, Laks maņa and Sītā, and appearing as if she had been dancing incessantly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.608,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4cff1a3d3284ea9bc13bee718693614cde703e621ace613c3e6bd9a87f148538","compact":"26b56a1385a35a16d86bcec8224623c7f2c318a59b3cfee6bc5f7f363e77499b","nasal":"d3b29b543220db722fa209cdaa2ffc894fa01d3dde004b24dd63faa3324a4322"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":33,"english":"The king exclaimed, \"Stay,” Rāghava said, \"On, On.\" Sumantra's mind vacillated like that of one placed between two hosts burning to encounter each other.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a6fe96b0b04f765169c0d067449f25d3fe42d7b48c47cd3990885f6466b6d36","compact":"74ae43c95879920d49ccfa7c5e424ba74209e98fa2f51bac88a6c9689de85dce","nasal":"98a5037fcd035fd8857b7cd4792649d5687b417132b9e352daa9a2888ae6cbff"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":34,"english":"Rāma said to him, “When taxed by the monarch (on your return), you will say, 'I did not hear you.' But delay will impart me terrible pain.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63f60242f19715417e453f0355067ecaf10877ff4e970a158b671b2a547d5930","compact":"9746d53ebf67ed77f1b261834c4c8ea0c5bf9c0a15379f7b7305b609e95714a8","nasal":"9746d53ebf67ed77f1b261834c4c8ea0c5bf9c0a15379f7b7305b609e95714a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":35,"english":"Thereupon, doing Rāma's bidding, the charioteer, telling the people to desist, made the horses already coursing, run faster.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.567,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc3d6bcd45efe9c879b8888cd855917f675911c98143ff059ef236bce90c8381","compact":"c53ac566defb4ad9cee61cf0ae66babbf2cc41db1ce3d476198fcd4c70c1ad12","nasal":"16810e90f87d80f11f804f3affd90b66282747cdfccf94c5d27511f138a891c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":35,"verse":36,"english":"The retainers of the king stopped after circumambulating Rāma, but their minds did not turn back. But the others did not return either bodily or mentally.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-40-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2035036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdef6876b386ccea69ee75cb3191eb6c70ce569eaacdfff328e852960d51f2f5","compact":"04f8b7eec98ce885f576c917a478390b42c9979c2d2972c7d48d8e6a61f5847f","nasal":"897d5c73607d36d0070fb0968c78bd4ea42dece7f9c4198649080bb576436d14"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-35-37","kanda":2,"kandaId"